rom Alaska, and he and Darwin find solace in each other, eventually deciding to marry.\n\n    *   *Man vs. Nature:* The struggle to tame the Nebraska prairie.\n    *   *Passion vs. Tradition:* The contrast between the refined/passionate (Charles, Max, Lenny) and the traditional/narrow (Darnell, Lara, Kora).\n    *   *Resilience and Strength:* Darwin's role as the pillar of the family.\n    *   *Love and Tragedy:* The destructive power of jealousy and the purity of a forbidden love.\n    *   *Cycle of Life:* The land remains while humans come and go.\n\n    *   *Introduction:* Set the scene in Nebraska.\n    *   *The Milan Family:* Describe Darwin's leadership and the family's struggle.\n    *   *The Tragedy:* Detail the relationship between Charles and Max and the resulting murder-suicide/crime of passion.\n    *   *The Resolution:* Describe Darwin's growth, her compassion for Kora, and her union with Lenny.\n    *   *Conclusion:* Reflect on the theme of the land."
